meta {
  name: Update and Delete Product Family
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/REPLACE_WITH_FAMILY_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against the disposable scratch family from
  "Create Product Family.bru" (id `6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e`) on
  "David's Dev Account". Like `POST`, `PATCH`/`DELETE` on
  `/product-families/{identifier}` are **brand-new** capabilities in the
  2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh, not previously-undeclared-but-
  working ones -- Phase 3 confirmed this resource had **zero** write
  capability at all (quirk #38). Confirmed live: both now genuinely work.

  ## What it does
  - `PATCH /product-families/{id}` -- `200`. `ProductFamilyUpdateInputDto`
    accepts **only `name`**, by design: the spec's own schema description
    explains attribute membership changes are excluded on purpose because
    they trigger an unbounded, destructive propagation across the
    family's products (deleting attribute values off variants whose
    parent now owns them) that must go through a Job, not a synchronous
    PATCH. Response is the full family shape (adds `created_at`,
    `created_user_audit`, `modified_user_audit` vs. the create response).
  - `DELETE /product-families/{id}` -- `204`, then `404` on a follow-up
    `GET`.
  - The generic subpath mechanism (`PATCH /product-families/{id}/{path}`,
    same convention as every other resource -- `{path}` names an
    Update-DTO field, body is that field's bare new value) also works:
    `PATCH /product-families/{id}/name` with a raw string body -- `200`,
    same effect as the root PATCH. **`POST` on that same subpath is
    explicitly rejected** -- `405 {"errors":[{"name":"MethodNotAllowed",
    "description":"POST is not allowed on this path."}]}`, even though
    `openapi_pimv3.json` declares `post` as one of the methods on
    `/product-families/{identifier}/{path}` -- a real spec-vs-live status
    code mismatch worth flagging (the spec claims a route exists that
    405s for every path tried).
  - Not separately re-tested here: whether `DELETE
    /product-families/{id}/{path}` has the same "ignores `{path}`, deletes
    the whole family" hazard already proven on products (quirk #31) and
    products' relationships (quirk #54, now safely fixed for the new
    dedicated relationships endpoint -- see `17-Product-Relationships/`).
    Treat it as equally dangerous until proven otherwise; don't suggest a
    scoped subpath DELETE for this resource in any docs.
}

example {
  name: Update Product Family - Success (PATCH root)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against the disposable scratch family, renaming it.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Product Family Renamed"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "created": "2026-09-15T16:28:02.086000+00:00",
            "created_at": "2026-09-15T16:28:02.086000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "id": "6aa97212a30ca5945169a21e",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T16:29:00.361586+00:00",
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "name": "WC Test Product Family Renamed",
            "total_attributes": 4,
            "total_models": 1,
            "total_products": 0
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

